// Package testing's exported surface is a single type — TestResult, a distinct
// named char-slice type — which lives entirely in testing.bni.  This
// implementation file carries no code — it
// exists only to give the otherwise type-only package a compiled MODULE, so the
// compiler emits its `__Package()` descriptor.  That descriptor is what lets
// testing be injected into the VM as a native builtin alongside the other
// pkg/builtins packages (interp/externs.bn builtinPkgs); without a module there
// is no `__Package` to bind, so a type-only package cannot be injected.
package "pkg/builtins/testing"
